    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1046">

                <pb facs="0877" n="867" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 [Gleysteen, Culver]: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Paddock</hi>)<anchor n="19" xml:id="d1046-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-22T18:00:00-05:00">April 22, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Re Dairen’s 108 April 15 and 109 April 16 to Dept, Dept has pursuant Dairen
                    recommendation latter reftel deferred instructing Moscow protest Gleysteen
                    detention pending reply Soviet Kommandatura Dairen. However Dept reluctant defer
                    this action more than stipulated 2 or 3 days; accordingly requests Dairen report
                    present status reply.</p>
                <p>Dept inclined concur Nanking tel 803 April 20 to Dept recommending fullest
                    publicity Gleysteen detention at time protest despatched Moscow FonOff and
                    requests urgently views Moscow Dairen re desirability this action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1046-f1" n="19" type="source" xml:id="d1046-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as No. 250 to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
